.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-NIGHT-LIGHT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-night-light
.Nd Night Light from the command line
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm status
.Nm
.Cm on | off | auto
.Nm
.Cm inhibit
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Fl -
.Ar command
.Op Ar arg ...
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks and tells
.Xr patina-compositor 1
about Night Light, which warms the screen in the evening by its
.Ic [night_light]
settings.
Night Light is only on the hardware: nested in another desktop, that
desktop's own applies, and
.Nm
says Night Light isn't served.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
Print whether it's on, the temperature in kelvin, the override, and why
anything is holding it off.
The default.
.It Cm on , off
Turn it on or off until the schedule next changes.
.It Cm auto
Follow the schedule again.
.It Cm inhibit
Hold it off while
.Ar command
runs, as a photo editor needing true colour would, giving
.Ar text
as the reason Settings shows, or the command's name without
.Fl -reason .
It comes back when the command exits, or if
.Nm
is killed.
If the compositor can't be reached, the command runs anyway.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
For
.Cm inhibit ,
the exit status of
.Ar command ,
or 127 when it can't be run.
Otherwise 0, or 1 when the compositor can't be reached.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ patina-night-light inhibit --reason \(dqEditing photos\(dq -- darktable
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-settings 1
